108:# !HLDA & !CLK16 & MRD                                                       /* CLK16 SYNC */
109:# !HLDA &  CLK16 & MRD  &  NAM 
110:#  HLDA &  W_R   & DMIO &  D_C & !ADSM & M32 & MRAS                          /* DMA READ (NOT REFRESH) */
111:#  HLDA &  MRD   & DMIO & !ADSM;                                             /* DMA READ HOLD */
112:                     
113:
114:
115:/*
116:DESCRIPTION
117:This PAL is used in the D4 (386) memory board to control the DRAM subsystem.
118:The RAS and CAS master strobes are generated, and the CPU next address and
119:READY signals are provided.
120:Rev A of this PAL changes the DMA state machine to prevent spurious RAM cycles
121:after refresh or DMA cycles.
122:
123:*/
124:
